Package: verterm
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: @URL@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= @GLIBC@), libgcc-s1, libssl3 | libssl3t64
Recommends: libxkbcommon0, libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1, libvulkan1, libegl1, fontconfig
Suggests: libxkbcommon-x11-0, libx11-6, libxcb1, libxcursor1, libxi6, git, xdg-utils, mako-notifier | dunst | sway-notification-center | notification-daemon
Description: GPU-accelerated, keyboard-centric terminal emulator
 verterm is a Wayland-first terminal emulator written in Rust on
 alacritty_terminal and egui/wgpu, built around a vertical tab tree instead of
 a horizontal tab bar.
 .
 A /proc scanner classifies every session as a local project, an SSH host, a
 container or a root shell, and keeps per-tab job health live: running or
 finished, exit code, CPU and RSS footprint, git branch. Desktop notifications
 fire over D-Bus when a long command finishes while its tab or the window is
 unfocused. Scrollback has a vi mode with search and yank, fast-jump hints for
 URLs, paths and hashes, and a session search that looks through both tab
 identity and what each tab has printed. A summon-only Ollama integration
 drafts shell commands; nothing it produces reaches a shell without an
 explicit keystroke.
 .
 The Recommends are dlopen'ed at runtime rather than linked, so they do not
 show up in the automatic shared-library dependencies: libxkbcommon for
 keyboard handling on both backends, the Wayland client libraries for the
 primary backend, and the Vulkan loader or libEGL for the wgpu renderer.
 fontconfig supplies fc-match, which resolves the configured font families;
 without it verterm falls back to egui's built-in faces. The Suggests are the
 X11 fallback backend and the optional integrations: git for branch badges,
 xdg-utils for opening URLs from fast-jump hints, and a notification daemon
 for desktop alerts.
